
# Episode 4 — The Silent Heroes of Our History (notes)

## Candidates

- William Yeager — Stanford staff engineer who wrote much of the software for Stanford's multiprotocol router (the "blue box") in the early 1980s, built to tie the campus's incompatible networks together. Cisco's first routers came from that work; Stanford licensed the software to Cisco in 1987 after a dispute with the founders. Yeager saw little of the fortune that followed. Recheck dates and the license terms against primary sources before scripting.
